00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.370 align:start position:0%
procrastination is a trap that many of  us fall into it usually involves  ignoring an unpleasant but likely more  important task in favor of one that is  more enjoyable or easier if we  procrastinate over a long period of time  we can become demotivated and  disillusioned with our work which can  even lead to depression and job loss  here are some tips to avoid  procrastination one plan and organize  you are more likely to procrastinate if  you don't have an organized plan or idea  for completing your work investing in  planning and organizing your work is a  good idea start keeping track of all  your work and assignments when you're  organized it gives you a more orderly  and measured framework within which to  work sure prioritize work prioritizing  your work and assignments is another way  to help you avoid procrastination make a  to-do list of what needs to be completed  make sure you address the most critical  or time-sensitive assignments first then  work your way down the list get the hard  stuff out of the way first so that  everything that comes after it will seem  more manageable three set deadlines  another tip to avoid procrastination is  to set deadlines many people get stuck  and I'll do it tomorrow or eventually  cycle when in truth that day or  eventually never comes it's important to  set a specific date for when you want a  project or assignment to be completed  and to complete your projects and  assignments before the deadline that way  if something unexpected happens you  still have extra time to complete them  4. eliminate all distractions getting  rid of distractions is one of the most  efficient way to avoid procrastination  by limiting the number of distractions  around you you're more likely to get  done what you need to do  shut your phone off Retreat to a quiet  place and listen to classical music or  white noise to drown out any noise and  do your task being focused and dedicated  finally 5. reward yourself rewarding  yourself May create an incentive to  complete a task and help avoid  procrastination after working hard or  after completing tasks consider giving  yourself a reward it could be as simple  as once I finish this assignment I can  watch an episode of my favorite show  this will be a reward to our efforts  which will give us positive  reinforcement and motivates us to work  more efficiently thank you for watching  And subscribe for more
 

